@crisbeto quick update: I was able to repro the issue locally, here is my diff:

```
--- a/packages/core/test/acceptance/discover_utils_spec.ts
+++ b/packages/core/test/acceptance/discover_utils_spec.ts
@@ -74,9 +74,16 @@ onlyInIvy('Ivy-specific utilities').describe('discovery utils', () => {
       <child dirA #child></child>
       <child dirA *ngIf="true"></child>
       <ng-container><p></p></ng-container>
+      <ng-container *ngIf="visible">
+        <b>
+          Bold
+          <u>Underline</u>
+        </b>
+      </ng-container>
     `
   })
   class MyApp {
+    visible = true;
     text: string = 'INIT';
     @Input('a') b = 2;
     @Output('c') d = new EventEmitter();
@@ -89,6 +96,14 @@ onlyInIvy('Ivy-specific utilities').describe('discovery utils', () => {
     }
   }
 
+  fit('try to use debug functions on removed elements', () => {
+    const u = fixture.nativeElement.querySelector('u');
+    const uTokens = getInjectionTokens(u);
+    fixture.componentInstance.visible = false;
+    fixture.detectChanges();
+    const uTokens2 = getInjectionTokens(u);  // <-- this will throw
+  });
```

The problem is that the first `getInjectionTokens` call creates a new `LContext` for the `<u>` element (as it walks up the parent tree in `readPatchedData`), which also contains an `lViewId` reference. Once the view gets removed and the necessary cleanup happens (thus an `lView` with a previously stored id can not be found in the map) and we try to invoke the `getInjectionTokens` function again, we try to pull an `lView` using id that no longer has corresponding value in the map. Prior to the change in this PR, there was a direct `LView` reference, so the problem didn't happen. Now we would not be able to establish this connection and retrieve any info using DOM elements removed from the tree. This makes sense to me that the debug info is not available for removed elements, but there might be some code that relies on this (we'd need to run a global presubmit) and also that might be  a change in behavior between Ivy and ViewEngine.

It looks like we need to account for this case (that `lViewId` may point to a removed `lView`) in the code and replace an assert that verifies that the `context.lView` is an instance of an `LView` with a check that would return the default value for a particular function (an empty array or `null`).

Thank you.

